{
  "requirement": "requirements.ci.errors",
  "file": "src/evidence.rs",
  "item": "fn[validate_evidence_file]",
  "queries": [
    "early_exits",
    "error_accumulators"
  ],
  "applies": true,
  "fixmes": [],
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "`src/evidence.rs#fn[validate_evidence_file]` takes an `errors: &mut Vec<String>` parameter, so it is a site of `requirements.ci.errors`.\n\nThe four early-exit violation matches are all `return`s that follow a file-level parse or decoding failure:\n- `fs::read_to_string` fails.\n- `serde_json::from_str` fails.\n- `evidence_format::application_fields` returns an error.\n- The value is not a JSON object.\n\nThe requirement says an unparseable evidence file is one failed check and its error MAY report only the first parse or decoding problem. Each of these returns pushes exactly one error and stops. Every later field check needs the parsed object, so none of them can run without it. The requirement does not allow skipping any other check, and these returns skip none. All four matches are harmless.\n\nOnce the record is a well-formed object, the function does not return early. It runs these checks in turn, each pushing its own error:\n- `check_native`\n- `check_keys`\n- the `references` digest check\n- the text-field checks\n- the determination check\n- the rationale check\n- the false-determination check\n- `validate_dependencies` for orphaned records\n- `validate_input` for every input in the loop\n\nA failure in one of these does not stop the later checks. Checks that depend on a result are handled correctly. For example, the text comparison and the \"determination is false\" message run only when the corresponding field was obtained.\n\nI found no failure reported twice. `check_keys` reports only unexpected keys. Missing or mistyped fields are reported once, by `string_field` or by the determination `match`. The empty-text, text-changed, empty-rationale and false-determination messages each describe a distinct failed check.\n\nThe site meets its obligations.",
  "inputs": [
    {
      "file": "src/evidence.rs",
      "item": "fn[validate_evidence_file]",
      "hash": "06aee80cdc5e4955408999608ed902ba5c094d70c781808fa8847899dfb3dad7"
    },
    {
      "requirements": "requirements.ci.errors",
      "matches": [
        "requirements.ci.errors"
      ],
      "text": [
        ":::::{req} errors",
        "Repository validation MUST continue after a failed check and report every failed",
        "check it finds in one run, each as a {term}`requirements.ci.validation_error`.",
        "This is a convention for every validation error; the requirement for each check",
        "states which conditions that check reports. A file that cannot be parsed, such as",
        "a malformed `habeas.toml`, `book.toml`, or evidence file, is one failed check:",
        "its error MAY report only the first parse or decoding problem in that file, and",
        "checks that do not depend on its contents MUST still run.",
        "",
        "The code that sequences the repository's checks carries out the first paragraph.",
        "A repository-validation function that collects validation errors MUST hold them",
        "in a parameter or local variable named `errors`, and a function with such a",
        "variable is a site below; authoring code that collects errors only to abort is",
        "not one. After one of its checks fails, a site MUST still run every later check",
        "that does not depend on the failed check's result, including later checks in the",
        "same loop iteration, and MUST NOT report one failure twice.",
        "",
        "::::{sites} error_accumulators",
        "```yaml",
        "language: rust",
        "paths: [src, crates/trust-but-verify/src]",
        "exclude: [src/authoring/inputs.rs, src/authoring/tools.rs]",
        "rule:",
        "  kind: function_item",
        "  has:",
        "    stopBy: { kind: function_item }",
        "    any:",
        "      - kind: parameter",
        "        has: { field: pattern, regex: \"^errors$\" }",
        "      - kind: let_declaration",
        "        has: { field: pattern, regex: \"^errors$\" }",
        "  not:",
        "    inside:",
        "      stopBy: end",
        "      kind: mod_item",
        "      has: { field: name, regex: \"^tests$\" }",
        "match:",
        "  - \"fn check(value: &str, errors: &mut Vec<String>) {}\"",
        "  - |",
        "    fn run() {",
        "        let mut errors: BTreeSet<String> = BTreeSet::new();",
        "        check(\"\", &mut errors);",
        "    }",
        "no_match:",
        "  - \"fn check(value: &str, discovery_errors: &mut Vec<String>) {}\"",
        "  - |",
        "    fn run() {",
        "        let mut problems = Vec::new();",
        "        check(\"\", &mut problems);",
        "    }",
        "  - |",
        "    mod tests {",
        "        fn check(errors: &mut Vec<String>) {}",
        "    }",
        "```",
        "::::",
        "",
        "::::{violations} early_exits",
        "```yaml",
        "language: rust",
        "paths: [src, crates/trust-but-verify/src]",
        "within: error_accumulators",
        "rule:",
        "  any:",
        "    - kind: try_expression",
        "    - kind: return_expression",
        "    - kind: continue_expression",
        "    - kind: break_expression",
        "match:",
        "  - |",
        "    fn check(v: &Value, errors: &mut Vec<String>) -> Option<u8> {",
        "        let n = v.as_u64()?;",
        "        if v.is_null() { errors.push(\"null\".into()); }",
        "        Some(n as u8)",
        "    }",
        "  - |",
        "    fn check(items: &[Value], errors: &mut Vec<String>) {",
        "        for item in items {",
        "            if !item.is_object() { errors.push(\"object\".into()); continue; }",
        "            if item.is_null() { errors.push(\"null\".into()); }",
        "        }",
        "    }",
        "  - |",
        "    fn check(v: &Value, errors: &mut Vec<String>) {",
        "        if !v.is_object() { errors.push(\"object\".into()); return; }",
        "        if v.is_null() { errors.push(\"null\".into()); }",
        "    }",
        "  - |",
        "    fn check(items: &[Value], errors: &mut Vec<String>) {",
        "        for item in items {",
        "            if !item.is_object() { errors.push(\"object\".into()); break; }",
        "        }",
        "        if items.is_empty() { errors.push(\"empty\".into()); }",
        "    }",
        "no_match:",
        "  - |",
        "    fn parse(v: &Value) -> Option<u8> {",
        "        let n = v.as_u64()?;",
        "        Some(n as u8)",
        "    }",
        "```",
        "::::",
        ":::::"
      ]
    },
